#====================================================================
# E244 — Handle operation errors must be captured before close
#====================================================================

id:                     E244
trigger_tool:           conan_test|ctest|runtime|c-api
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        operation returned failure but reported error is zero|last operation error lost after close|error reporting dereferences a closed handle

severity:               2
category:               testing|c-api|error-contract|resource-lifetime
match_keywords:         handle error, out parameter, last operation error, close error, error lifetime, fault injection, use after close
title:                  Capture handle operation errors before closing resources

root_cause:             Some C libraries report open and close failures through an out-parameter but store errors from operations on an already-open resource inside the live handle. Reusing the open out-parameter for operation failures reports a stale success value. Closing first can overwrite the out-parameter and free the handle, making later error access invalid.
affected_scope:         Stateful C APIs whose open/close calls use error out-parameters while read, write, parse, encode, or decode calls store their last error in a live handle or context object.
verification_cmd:       Run separate consumers that force an operation failure after a successful open and require the live handle error to be nonzero before close.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           operation-fault-injection-with-pre-close-error-snapshot
rec_description:        Give open, operation, and close errors separate variables. After an operation returns failure, read or snapshot the documented handle error before closing. Use deterministic fault fixtures in separate consumer processes and verify that the open error remains success while the operation error is nonzero.
rec_command:            conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<target-profile> -pr:b=<target-profile> --build='*'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               public-api-error-lifetime-consumers

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      documented-error-field-audit
fallback_description:   If deterministic target fault injection is unavailable, verify the installed public header and implementation contract, but record runtime error-lifetime coverage as pending.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       operation.*failed.*open_error|close.*then.*handle.*error|free.*then.*error
forbid_1_reason:        The open out-parameter does not own later operation failures, and a closed handle may already be freed.
forbid_1_consequence:   Diagnostics report zero or the close result, or access freed memory, hiding the original failure.
forbid_2_pattern:       happy.path.*only|mock.*error.*without.*real.*public.api
forbid_2_reason:        A successful round trip does not execute the error ownership contract, and a mock cannot prove the library's real state transition.
forbid_2_consequence:   Error handling remains untested even though normal encoding or decoding passes.

principles:
